WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.761
A join should be validated before its result is used
for reporting

00:00:03.774 --> 00:00:09.579
or analysis Start with row counts How many rows

00:00:09.605 --> 00:00:12.540
were in each input and how many rows are in the
output

00:00:14.271 --> 00:00:18.629
Then count distinct keys If the final grain should
be one row

00:00:18.642 --> 00:00:24.221
per patient compare total rows with distinct patient
IDs If those numbers

00:00:24.247 --> 00:00:30.232
differ investigate why Inspect keys with unusually
many matches

00:00:31.169 --> 00:00:35.025
A patient with many admissions or labs is useful for
understanding whether

00:00:35.038 --> 00:00:40.657
multiplication is expected Also spot-check at least
two known cases

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.539
one entity with multiple related rows and one entity
with no related

00:00:44.565 --> 00:00:50.437
row Finally write the grain sentence For example

00:00:50.687 --> 00:00:55.950
one row represents one patient with summarized
activity counts If the query

00:00:55.976 --> 00:00:59.634
output cannot be explained with a clear grain
sentence the join logic

00:00:59.647 --> 00:01:04.755
may still be ambiguous These checks are simple but
they catch a

00:01:04.781 --> 00:01:06.886
large share of real-world join errors
